# Hydromart internal sweeps (busybox crond). Times are the container's TZ (UTC by
# default — set TZ on the scheduler service to shift). Logs go to the container.
#
# Place orders for all due recurring subscriptions — hourly.
0 * * * * sh /scripts/sweep.sh subscriptions/process-due
# "Time to refill" reorder reminders — daily at 08:00.
0 8 * * * sh /scripts/sweep.sh orders/reminders/reorder
# Retention enforcement (M23-21): runs the policy for every dataset that has an executor
# — including proof-of-delivery, which used to sweep itself at 03:15 off a separate
# per-depot window. One owner for the rule now. Datasets with no executor are logged as
# such. Daily at 03:30, after the 03:00 database backup, so a bad delete is always
# recoverable from that night's dump.
30 3 * * * sh /scripts/sweep.sh retention/internal/purge admin:3017
# Release HR announcements whose scheduledAt has come due (C1). Every 15 minutes: the
# console lets HR pick a time to the minute, and an hourly sweep would make "kirim jam 9"
# arrive at 10. Nothing is sent twice — publishedAt is the latch.
*/15 * * * * sh /scripts/sweep.sh announcements/publish-due hr:3018
# Broadcast campaigns (B-17): send the next batch for every campaign still SENDING. The
# send endpoint only CLAIMS the campaign now — this sweep is what actually messages
# customers. Every 2 minutes: staff press "kirim" and expect it to be moving, not to wait
# an hour. Each tick is bounded and resumable, so an interrupted sweep loses nothing.
*/2 * * * * sh /scripts/sweep.sh campaigns/internal/process-sending crm:3012
# Partner webhook fan-out (H-30): send every delivery whose next attempt is due. Every
# 5 minutes rather than hourly — a partner integration that learns about a delivery an
# hour late is not an integration. Retries back off on their own (1m, 5m, 25m, ...), so
# a dead endpoint is not hammered by this cadence.
*/5 * * * * sh /scripts/sweep.sh webhooks/deliveries/process admin:3017
